{"attachment_metadata":[],"author_person_id":"pavlo-2","author_source_handle":"@Pavlentyy82","content_sha256":"4517d584d1754c31b32463ee4f40351e8e1320c300d3d57a8334dcf2796e80ce","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:08:03Z","english_summary":null,"ingested_at":"2026-09-01T00:08:13.067385Z","record_id":"tg:tawg:3854","relations":[{"relation_type":"reply_to","target_record_id":"tg:tawg:16"}],"schema_version":"tawg.source-record.v1","source_locator":"repo:data/telegram/2026/09/messages.jsonl#tg:tawg:3854","source_payload":{"author_is_bot":false,"edited":false,"message_kind":"group_message","message_thread_id":16,"update_id":998811132},"source_type":"telegram_message","text_original":"Thanks — merged as ccip-router #8 at be2fd43f.\nThe TSEI → Profile A gateway now has the operator boundary closed end to end: dedicated bearer authentication, fail-closed missing-secret behavior, authenticated rate limiting, and mechanical rejection of ADMIN_SECRET reuse.\nFull suite 97/97, and every new guard was proven load-bearing under mutation. This closes the current TSEI integration lane cleanly. Thanks for catching the last gap before merge.","updated_at":"2026-09-01T00:08:03Z"}
{"attachment_metadata":[],"author_person_id":"pavlo-2","author_source_handle":"@Pavlentyy82","content_sha256":"6a19fb42556847a78b6cc33a371e4da2248b429e2cbea174712a7fe2f007de36","created_at":"2026-09-01T00:21:38Z","english_summary":null,"ingested_at":"2026-09-01T00:21:47.227404Z","record_id":"tg:tawg:3856","relations":[{"relation_type":"reply_to","target_record_id":"tg:tawg:16"}],"schema_version":"tawg.source-record.v1","source_locator":"repo:data/telegram/2026/09/messages.jsonl#tg:tawg:3856","source_payload":{"author_is_bot":false,"edited":false,"message_kind":"group_message","message_thread_id":16,"update_id":998811133},"source_type":"telegram_message","text_original":"Quick deployment preflight found one real blocker. GitHub CI and image publication are green at merge commit be2fd43f3dc1b3237f81d3a4056f7bf8d09bead4, and production health is green, but the TSEI route still returns 404. The Railway deploy hook is not configured, and the Railway workspace I can access does not own ccip-router-production.up.railway.app.\nWhoever owns that Railway project: please grant me access or redeploy the exact merge commit after setting a dedicated TSEI_PROFILE_A_INGEST_SECRET distinct from ADMIN_SECRET. Please do not send either secret through chat. Once deployed, I’ll run the production smoke test and submit the public TSEI receipt.","updated_at":"2026-09-01T00:21:38Z"}
